# Day 11/60 — ATS Resume Optimization for a Specific Job Description

## Objective

Learn how to optimize a resume for a specific job description instead of using a generic resume for every application.

## Task

1. Upload resume
2. Select a target Job Description (JD)
3. Run ATS analysis using Claude
4. Review ATS match score
5. Identify keyword and skill gaps
6. Generate an optimized resume

## What I Learned

### ATS Systems Compare Resumes to Job Descriptions

Many recruiters use ATS software before manually reviewing applications.

The ATS evaluates:

* Keywords
* Skills
* Experience alignment
* Job relevance

### Resume Customization Matters

A single resume cannot perfectly match every role.

Customizing the resume for a target position improves relevance and ATS performance.

### AI Can Accelerate Optimization

Claude helped:

* Identify missing keywords
* Highlight skill gaps
* Improve role alignment
* Generate a stronger ATS-friendly version

## Biggest Insight

A good resume gets noticed.

A resume aligned with the job description gets shortlisted.

## Key Takeaway

Resume + Job Description + ATS Optimization = Better Application Strategy

